  "title": "Network of autoscopic hallucinations elicited by intracerebral stimulation of periventricular nodular heterotopia: SEEG during 43 Hz and single-pulse stimulation (1 patient)",
  "description": "Stereo-EEG recordings from a single patient with drug-resistant epilepsy and a right posterior temporal periventricular nodular heterotopia (PVNH). 43 Hz high-frequency stimulation of the PVNH elicited autoscopic hallucinations, and single-pulse electrical stimulation was used to map effective connectivity. The dataset supports multi-modal connectivity analysis of the network underlying the hallucinations, which involves the PVNH, occipital and temporal neocortex, fusiform gyrus and parietal cortex.",
  "methods_description": "SEEG was recorded at 4096 Hz with 148 channels (128 SEEG channels) on an XLTek Quantum system using Dixi depth electrodes. Bipolar stimulation of PVNH contacts D08-D09 used an FHC Guideline 4000LP+ stimulator. High-frequency stimulation was 43.3 Hz biphasic with alternating polarity, delivered for 5 s at 0.25-3 mA. Single-pulse stimulation used 20 pulses per trial with a 15 s inter-stimulus interval. A defaced T1 MRI and contact coordinates are included.",
